-- title:
--   Invariant idèle classes are norms from the compositum
-- statement:
--   Let $E$, $F$, $L$, $N$ be number fields with $E$-algebra structures on $F$, $L$, $N$ and $N$ an algebra over both $F$ and $L$, compatibly with the towers $E \subseteq F \subseteq N$ and $E \subseteq L \subseteq N$, with $F/E$, $L/E$ and $N/E$ Galois. Let $D$ be a descent datum for $N/E$ on the adèles of $N$: a homomorphism from $N \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} N$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathrm{AdeleRing}(\mathcal O_N, N)$, continuous in each variable and satisfying $D.\mathrm{act}\,g(\iota x) = \iota(g x)$ for $x \in N$, where $\iota$ is the structure map. The group $N \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} N$ is assumed to act multiplicatively on the idèle class group $\mathrm{IdeleClassGroup}(\mathcal O_N, N) = (\mathrm{AdeleRing}(\mathcal O_N, N))^\times / \mathrm{principalIdeles}$, with $\mathrm{principalIdeles}$ the image of $N^\times$ in the idèles, and this action is assumed (hypothesis `hact`) to coincide with the one induced on the quotient by $D$ through `IdeleGaloisDescent.classAct`. Let $S$, $T$ be normal subgroups with $S$ the set of elements fixing $\iota(F)$ pointwise and $T$ the set of elements fixing $\iota(L)$ pointwise, and assume $S \cap T = 1$. Assume further that the quotient by $T$ is generated by a single element $s$ whose order divides the cardinality of the quotient by $S$, and that $S$ is generated by a single element $t$. Then, in the additively written $\mathbb Z$-linear representation `Rep.ofMulDistribMulAction` attached to this action, for every $a_0$ fixed by $\rho(g)$ for all $g$ there exists $b$ with $\sum_{i=0}^{\mathrm{ord}(t)-1} \rho(t^i)\,b = a_0$; multiplicatively, $a_0$ is a norm from the cyclic group generated by $t$.
--
--   This is the statement that every $\mathrm{Gal}(N/E)$-invariant idèle class of $N$ lies in the image of the norm for $\mathrm{Gal}(N/F)$, in the coordinates of a compositum $N = FL$ with an auxiliary cyclic layer $L/E$ of degree dividing $[F:E]$, as in Artin and Tate's construction of the fundamental class. It supplies the norm-surjectivity hypothesis used by [`M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup) and its $p$-group variant.
